=== 64: A special builtin's usage and assignment errors are fatal in POSIX mode
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|status 2: set -o bogus
|status 2: set --bogus
|status 2: trap -Z
|status 2: shift abc
|status 1: readonly 1x
|status 1: export 1x=2 y=3
|status 1: readonly r=1; readonly r=2
|status 1: readonly r=1; unset r
|status 1: readonly r=1; export r=2
|status 1: . /nonexistent-file
|status 2: f() { return abc; }; f
|status 2: return 3
|status 2: exec -Z
|status 2: export --help >/dev/null
|status 2: for i in 1; do break abc; done
--- stderr
|bash: line 2: set: bogus: invalid option name
|bash: line 4: set: --: invalid option
|set: usage: set [-abefhkmnptuvxBCEHPT] [-o option-name] [--] [-] [arg ...]
|bash: line 6: trap: -Z: invalid option
|trap: usage: trap [-Plp] [[action] signal_spec ...]
|bash: line 8: shift: abc: numeric argument required
|bash: line 10: readonly: `1x': not a valid identifier
|bash: line 12: export: `1x=2': not a valid identifier
|bash: line 14: r: readonly variable
|bash: line 16: unset: r: cannot unset: readonly variable
|bash: line 18: r: readonly variable
|bash: line 20: /nonexistent-file: No such file or directory
|bash: line 22: return: abc: numeric argument required
|bash: line 24: return: can only `return' from a function or sourced script
|bash: line 26: exec: -Z: invalid option
|exec: usage: exec [-cl] [-a name] [command [argument ...]] [redirection ...]
|bash: line 30: break: abc: numeric argument required

=== 65: A special builtin's ordinary failures are not fatal in POSIX mode
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|survived 1: trap x BOGUS
|survived 1: set -- a; shift 3
|survived 1: export -f nofunc
|survived 1: unset -f -v x
|survived 0: unset 1x
|survived 1: for i in 1; do break 0; done
|survived 0: break
|survived 0: continue 2
--- stderr
|bash: line 4: trap: BOGUS: invalid signal specification
|bash: line 4: shift: 3: shift count out of range
|bash: line 4: export: nofunc: not a function
|bash: line 4: unset: cannot simultaneously unset a function and a variable
|bash: line 4: break: 0: loop count out of range

